From 27223ac4d4c21096a7fcca23c319be92b57f3e1d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "xiu.yang" <xiu.yang@sophgo.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 16:16:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(ab): select the boot slot from the misc partition with
 fallback

[description ]:
- cmd/cvi_boot_mode.c, include/cvi_boot_mode.h (new, CONFIG_CMD_BOOT_MODE,
  built for SPL and u-boot): read/write the AvbABData A/B record stored in
  the raw NAND "misc" partition (AB_MISC_OFFSET/AB_MISC_SIZE from
  cvipart.h, first good block, erase+write+verify, bad block skipping);
  pick the bootable slot with the highest priority, decrement its
  tries_remaining, init defaults when the record is invalid; commands
  ab_select (sets ${root}/${ab_boot_part} for nandboot), get_slot,
  set_slot a|b, dump_abdata, reinit_abdata.
- common/spl/spl_nand.c: with CONFIG_AB_SYSTEM the fast boot path loads
  the kernel from boot_a/boot_b according to the misc record; when the
  FIT cannot be loaded the slot is marked unbootable (tries=0) and the
  other slot is loaded in the same run. CONFIG_B_SYSTEM without
  AB_SYSTEM selects boot_b at build time.
- common/fdt_support.c: SPL bootargs built per selected slot
  (cvi_ab_spl_bootargs).
- include/configs/cv181x-asic.h: ROOTARGS from ROOTFS_DEV/ROOTFS_DEV_B
  (ROOTARGSA/ROOTARGSB with slot_suffix=_a/_b), nandboot reads
  ${ab_boot_part} after ab_select, CVI_SPL_BOOTAGRS_NOROOT; legacy
  BOOT/ROOTFS names remain the default.
- cvitek.mk: pass CONFIG_AB_SYSTEM/CONFIG_B_SYSTEM from the SDK config.
- drivers/mtd/nand/raw/cvitek/cvsnfc_spl.c: export the SPL mtd
  (cvsnfc_spl_get_mtd). cvsnfc.c: report page program / block erase
  failure (STATUS_P_FAIL/E_FAIL) so misc writes can detect bad blocks.
- cmd/cvi_update.c: SET_DL_COMPLETE uses the SRAM flag when the env is
  not stored (CONFIG_ENV_IS_NOWHERE) instead of calling saveenv.
- cmd/Kconfig, cmd/Makefile, scripts/config_whitelist.txt: wiring.

[root   cause]:
- The SPL fast boot path always loaded the kernel from a single fixed
  BOOT offset and the bootargs named a fixed ROOTFS partition, so a
  damaged kernel/rootfs could not be recovered and A/B switching was not
  possible. BF01 (SPI NAND, fast boot without full u-boot) needs the
  decision inside the SPL.
- Boards without an ENV partition printed "Unknown command 'saveenv'"
  after USB download because SET_DL_COMPLETE only checked
  CONFIG_CMD_SAVEENV.

[JIRA      ID]:TBD-BF01-AB (to be provided)
[chip project]:181x
[side effects]:
- All new code is under CONFIG_AB_SYSTEM / CONFIG_B_SYSTEM /
  CONFIG_CMD_BOOT_MODE; other boards are unaffected. cvsnfc now returns
  an error on program/erase failure instead of silently succeeding.
- CONFIG_SPL_RAW_IMAGE_SUPPORT must be disabled on A/B boards, otherwise
  an erased boot slot is executed as a raw image (board defconfig).
- Verified on cv1815ja_bf01_spinand: slot A/B boot, slot switch from
  Linux, erased boot_b -> fallback to A, USB download without saveenv
  error.

[Affected *.ko/*.so/*.a] :fip_spl.bin / fip.bin (u-boot-spl, u-boot); no .ko/.so/.a

